WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.290
Welcome to the Transhuman Daily, Tuesday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.030
Here's your day in transhumanism, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.010
Up to speed! Google DeepMind's AI agents found faster quantum algorithms,

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:21.520
and proved every one.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:24.730
And a rare muscle-wasting disease got its firs

00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:27.430
t approved drug; patients on it walked faster.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:35.130
A brain implant gives Mary a voice. With Nvidia,

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.980
its computer cart should shrink to a box.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.430
Anthropic's Claude can now fix failing code checks itself,

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:45.100
and approve routine changes if teams allow.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:48.960
Meta's AI chief says superintelligence is arriving,

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:51.680
and warns against handing society over to it.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:56.540
And philosopher Thomas Nagel, famous for his bat essay,

00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:59.330
says fluent words don't make AI conscious.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.810
On to longevity. In half a million Britons,

00:01:02.810 --> 00:01:06.530
the dirtiest air came with a quarter more dementia risk.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.110
And a Cambridge study found leukaemia's first mutation often appears before age 20,

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:14.860
decades before diagnosis.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.530
Scientists built digital twins of almost 7,000 brains,

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:21.600
to see how ageing and surroundings shape them.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.460
Closer to home, after South Australia relaxed medical checks for older drivers,

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:29.470
their crash rate actually fell.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:33.820
On to wellbeing. Across 5,000 singles in 5 countries,

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:36.700
feeling free went with feeling happier.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.060
Meanwhile,

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:43.300
1 in 4 students at Bath turned to AI for mental-health support; more among those struggling.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:45.960
Now, the catch.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:52.320
Australia's health minister ordered an inquiry into peptides sold online as anti-ageing shortcuts.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.550
And a preprint found top AI models steering robot

00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:58.590
s often did harm in tests; a safety leash helped.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:02.880
On the frontier,

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.360
a drone folds its springy arms to squeeze through gaps half its width.

00:02:08.910 --> 00:02:12.000
A fungus that thrives at Chernobyl inspired tiny sphe

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.160
res that break down a nerve-agent stand-in in minutes.

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:19.610
And Munich's self-reflective robots simply stop when unsure,

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:21.940
then learn the new move from a human.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.160
Faster maths, faster legs,

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:27.980
and robots that know when to brake. Now you're up to speed!

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.550
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.440
And the future keeps arriving ahead of schedule.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.970
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.340
That's the Transhuman Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:51.140
Live long. See you tomorrow.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:56.600
Want more? Meet us in North Sydney on November 27.
